select public.prepify_load_bank('Computer Science', 2, $j$[["\"How to stop infectious diseases?\" is a real-world problem belonging to which field?",["Economic","Education","Healthcare","Transportation"],"C",3,0,"31cbc2c1a8cc"],["In computer science, a \"computing problem\" is specifically defined as a problem that is solved:",["Only by using the internet.","Step-by-step using computation.","By a human without a machine.","Instantly without any steps."],"B",3,0,"ed21a0d2fd91"],["When checking if a specific number is \"Prime\" or \"Not Prime,\" you are dealing with which type of computing problem?",["Search Problem","Decision Problem","Counting Problem","Abstraction Problem"],"B",3,0,"6a8893c1178b"],["In a \"Search Problem,\" which element represents the specific moves that transition from one node to another?",["Initial State","Operations","Goal","Decision Diamond"],"B",3,0,"23457bed8c15"],["To solve a search problem, the \"target of end condition\" is officially known as the:",["Initial State","Operation","Goal","Start State"],"C",3,0,"042ebeb44932"],["If you have 5 shirts and 3 pants, how many \"total possible casual dresses\" can you form?",["8","15","53","2"],"B",3,0,"e7d4b6ab730b"],["If you enter your home and see water on the floor, what do you need to solve such problems?",["High-speed internet access","Reasoning skills that are based on evidence and facts","A calculator to measure the volume of water","Advanced programming knowledge"],"B",3,0,"295bf22eb22f"],["In the I-P-O model, which term refers specifically to the \"requirements from the environment\"?",["Input","Process","Output","Storage"],"A",3,0,"b2d4e93689d9"],["For a programmer, an I-P-O chart is considered to be a:",["Type of hardware.","Handy tool to solve problems.","Decision problem.","Form of machine code."],"B",3,1,"7291e215585f"],["In an I-P-O chart, the \"Process\" column is defined as:",["Data entered into the system.","Operations that will be applied on the input.","Data that has been turned into information.","The hardware used for the computation."],"B",3,0,"5ad5b0b69e91"],["If you are calculating the \"Average of 5 numbers,\" the division operation would be listed in which section of the I-P-O chart?",["Input","Process","Output","Storage"],"B",3,0,"ac3f7b91be03"],["What is the official definition of \"Output\" in the I-P-O tabular form?",["Requirements from the environment.","Operations applied to the data.","Data that has been turned into the Information.","The physical screen of the computer."],"C",3,0,"38c432467c03"],["\"Computational Thinking\" is often described as an extension of which type of thinking?",["Mathematical Thinking","Logical Thinking","Creative Thinking","Fast Thinking"],"B",3,0,"90b423e58637"],["Which property of computational thinking involves \"removing the unnecessary details\" to focus on essential info?",["Decomposition","Abstraction","Pattern Recognition","Algorithm Design"],"B",3,0,"5cffaee82f48"],["The process of \"examining a problem for similarities between previously solved problems\" is:",["Decomposition","Abstraction","Pattern Recognition","Algorithm Design"],"C",3,0,"f5d1de47cf3e"],["\"Actual designing of solution\" and \"creating step-by-step plan\" defines:",["Logical Thinking","Algorithm Design","I-P-O Modeling","Problem Analysis"],"B",3,0,"843da82e75a9"],["In the \"Video Game\" example, ignoring the \"weather\" while focusing on the \"exit\" is an example of:",["Decomposition","Abstraction","Logical Thinking","Input Identification"],"B",3,0,"9e12853f10bf"],["Treating \"Six enemies as a single enemy\" because they behave the same way is an example of:",["Decomposition","Abstraction","Pattern Recognition","Search Problem"],"C",3,0,"98cbca9cb604"],["What is the benefit of developing \"algorithmic thinking skills\"?",["You become a hardware engineer.","You become a better problem solver.","You can type 100 words per minute.","You no longer need a computer."],"B",3,0,"3c766d8e8a64"],["Which solution design method is described as a \"diagrammatic representation of an algorithm\"?",["Flowchart","Concept Map","I-P-O Model","Machine Code"],"A",3,0,"48f2b7f4cb63"],["Every flowchart should officially start with a \"trigger,\" which is represented by which shape?",["Rectangle","Parallelogram","Oval shape","Diamond"],"C",3,0,"762f72af8eca"],["Which graphical shape represents the \"Input to the flowchart\"?",["Oval","Parallelogram","Rectangle","Diamond"],"B",3,0,"68315839bd0e"],["When a formula (like Area = (Base x Height) / 2) is applied in a flowchart, which symbol is used?",["Oval","Parallelogram","Rectangle","Diamond"],"C",3,0,"d6b58b88e32c"],["When a flowchart needs to check a condition (like \"Is Grade > 50?\"), which symbol is used?",["Rectangle","Diamond","Oval","Circle"],"B",3,0,"b597eab241a7"],["Why might a flowchart have \"multiple ends\"?",["Because the programmer got confused.","Because of the possibility of multiple decision points.","Because it is a complex search problem.","Because the trigger was not an oval."],"B",3,0,"aedd090c0c79"],["Which software tool is mentioned as famous for drawing various types of diagrams, including flowcharts?",["LARP","Microsoft Visio","Canva","ChatGPT"],"B",3,0,"7a09d8f15270"],["The LARP programming language is unique because it uses:",["Only binary code (0s and 1s).","Semi-natural syntax.","Only graphical icons.","Complex machine language."],"B",3,0,"18ff41194b30"],["In the \"Video Game Development\" concept map, what are the three sub-concepts under \"Game Design\"?",["Gameplay Mechanics, Level Design, and Storyline.","Coding, Scripting, and Engines.","2D Art, 3D Models, and Animation.","Sound Effects, Music, and Voice Acting."],"A",3,0,"a09ed3022b67"],["Which of the following methods are mentioned for designing a solution?",["Flowcharts and Source Code","Concept Maps and Pseudo-code","Flowcharts and Concept Maps","Algorithms and Charts"],"C",3,0,"3205754681b7"],["A developer divides a complex payroll system into employee records, salary calculation and report generation before implementation. Which computational thinking skill is being applied?",["Pattern recognition","Decomposition","Debugging","Selection"],"B",3,1,"5d026e3c8f31"],["An algorithm repeats the same instructions forever without ever reaching its final step. Which characteristic of a good algorithm has been violated?",["Effectiveness","Finiteness","Clarity","Input"],"B",5,1,"bee02fe0f9cf"],["Which situation is best classified as a computational problem rather than an ordinary daily-life problem?",["Choosing a dress for a party","Calculating the shortest route between two cities using a computer","Watering plants in a garden","Cleaning a classroom"],"B",3,0,"89cd78400497"],["An algorithm calculates the average age of four students. Which condition must the input satisfy for the result to be meaningful?",["Ages must be whole numbers","The input ages must be positive","The sum must be divisible by 4","The data must be sorted"],"B",5,1,"72d79652573d"],["A program checks whether water has reached 100 °C before displaying \"Boiling\". Which computational thinking skill is mainly used?",["Logical reasoning","Random guessing","Pattern recognition","Sequencing"],"A",3,1,"57209756d201"],["A teacher wants the total number of students who scored above 80 in a class. This problem is best classified as a:",["Decision problem","Search problem","Counting problem","Sorting problem"],"C",3,1,"6f2fc0bbc0fb"],["A program must check whether a student's marks are 50 or more before displaying \"Pass\". Which flowchart symbol represents this condition?",["Parallelogram","Rectangle","Diamond","Oval"],"C",1,1,"41f0b043f2ac"],["Which problem needs a \"Yes\" or \"No\" answer rather than locating or counting an item?",["Find a student's roll number","Count the absent students","Decide whether a student has paid the fee","Arrange students alphabetically"],"C",3,0,"c16a4354af9a"],["Which computational thinking skill is most directly responsible for spotting a solution that can be reused for similar problems?",["Algorithmic thinking","Pattern recognition","Abstraction","Decomposition"],"B",3,0,"8f79bd880873"],["In which situation is abstraction more appropriate than decomposition?",["Dividing a payroll system into modules","Ignoring students' favourite colours while designing a student database","Preparing steps to calculate percentages","Searching for a student's record"],"B",5,0,"26f422f7afa0"],["Which representation focuses on the sequence of operations rather than the relationships among ideas?",["Concept map","Flowchart","Mind map","Table"],"B",3,0,"c4ffcdd6a1cd"],["In which situation is logical thinking applied before algorithmic thinking?",["Deciding whether a voter is eligible based on age","Drawing flowchart symbols","Saving a program file","Installing software"],"A",5,0,"04033076674c"],["Which computational thinking property reduces a problem's complexity without dividing it into smaller parts?",["Pattern recognition","Abstraction","Decomposition","Sequencing"],"B",5,0,"317cfe29470c"],["Which task is least likely to be classified as a search problem?",["Locating a student's admission record","Finding a word in a dictionary","Deciding whether a password is valid","Searching for a contact number"],"C",5,0,"8d86418ab5a0"],["A programmer completes every processing step correctly but forgets to display the result. Which essential property of an algorithm is missing?",["Input","Output","Clarity","Finiteness"],"B",3,1,"7ad02b928a02"],["To calculate a student's total marks you split the program into: input the marks, calculate the sum, display the result. This splitting is known as:",["Pattern recognition","Decomposition","Abstraction","Debugging"],"B",3,1,"6ae9cdd61e0b"],["Which problem is most likely to need decomposition before an effective solution can be developed?",["Adding two numbers","Finding today's date","Developing a school management system","Switching on a computer"],"C",3,0,"908d6c612c43"],["A student first studies a problem carefully before applying any solution. According to the LARP approach, this stage is:",["Learning","Applying","Reflecting","Practising"],"A",3,1,"e2288aac8bed"],["A school's fee system is split into fee collection, fee calculation and report generation. Which computational thinking skill is being used?",["Abstraction","Decomposition","Pattern recognition","Sequencing"],"B",1,1,"bd8f75719ca5"],["Ali notices that every monthly electricity bill is calculated using the same formula. This observation demonstrates:",["Pattern recognition","Abstraction","Flowcharting","Sequencing"],"A",3,1,"8351434bf95b"],["While designing a student database, Sana ignores students' favourite colours because they are irrelevant. This is an example of:",["Decomposition","Abstraction","Sequencing","Testing"],"B",1,1,"bbed1ebe96cf"],["What is the output of this algorithm? Start; X = 1; print X; X = X + 2; if X < 6 go back to \"print X\"; End.",["1, 2, 3, 4, 5","1, 3, 5","1, 3, 5, 7","2, 4, 6"],"B",5,0,"a7d32910d628"],["A bank ATM follows a fixed sequence of instructions whenever cash is withdrawn. This sequence is known as:",["Data storage","An algorithm","An input device","A database"],"B",1,1,"27991b6481a6"],["A teacher asks students to identify common characteristics among birds, insects and mammals. Which computational thinking skill is being applied?",["Pattern recognition","Abstraction","Sequencing","Coding"],"A",3,1,"1cbfa1cd7bb5"],["In a flowchart for total marks, a student uses a diamond to check whether marks are greater than 50. The diamond represents a:",["Start/End","Process","Input/Output","Decision"],"D",1,1,"8583b48ca7ed"],["Students must show how \"Computer\", \"Hardware\", \"Software\" and \"Data\" are related, not the order of steps. Which tool should be used?",["Algorithm","Flowchart","Concept map","IPO chart"],"C",3,1,"4c5a6f23d96f"],["A company's online exam system has registration, paper generation, attendance and result modules, so the team divides it into smaller tasks first. This is mainly because the project is a:",["Simple problem","Logical problem","Counting problem","Complex problem"],"D",3,1,"26af2eaf700f"],["A weather department analyses millions of temperature readings every day to predict rainfall. Which type of problem is mainly being solved?",["Simple problem","Computational problem","Daily-life problem","Decision problem"],"B",3,1,"a42220043ecd"],["A programmer ignores unnecessary design details while developing a library management system. Which computational thinking concept is applied?",["Pattern recognition","Sequencing","Abstraction","Debugging"],"C",3,1,"6836dce5c9e8"],["Before coding, Ahmed draws a flowchart showing all the steps and decisions. The main purpose of the flowchart is to:",["Increase complexity","Graphically represent the algorithm","Store data permanently","Replace the program code"],"B",3,1,"fe726ca40a4b"],["Planning a school sports day is split into smaller tasks: booking the ground, making teams and arranging prizes. This skill is called:",["Abstraction","Decomposition","Pattern recognition","Debugging"],"B",3,1,"bd8f75719ca5"],["An algorithm must produce at least one result. This property is called:",["input","output","finiteness","definiteness"],"B",3,0,"7ad02b928a02"],["A librarian wants to know how many books were borrowed this week. This is best classified as a:",["sorting problem","counting problem","searching problem","decision problem"],"B",3,1,"6f2fc0bbc0fb"],["In a flowchart, the step \"Total = Price × Quantity\" is drawn inside a:",["diamond","rectangle","oval","parallelogram"],"B",3,0,"d6b58b88e32c"],["Which flowchart symbol is used for a question with a Yes/No answer, such as \"Is Age ≥ 18?\"",["Oval","Rectangle","Diamond","Parallelogram"],"C",1,0,"b597eab241a7"],["A city map shows the roads but leaves out trees and buildings. Which computational thinking skill does this show?",["Decomposition","Abstraction","Pattern recognition","Algorithm design"],"B",3,1,"5cffaee82f48"],["A student notices that the method for finding the average of test marks also works for average temperatures. This is:",["abstraction","pattern recognition","decomposition","debugging"],"B",3,1,"8f79bd880873"],["A diagram that shows the steps of an algorithm using standard symbols joined by arrows is a:",["concept map","flowchart","pseudocode","source code"],"B",1,0,"48f2b7f4cb63"],["In a search problem, the state we want to reach is called the:",["initial state","goal","operation","path"],"B",3,0,"042ebeb44932"],["In an I-P-O chart, the marks a student types into a result program are the:",["input","process","output","storage"],"A",3,1,"b2d4e93689d9"],["Which flowchart symbol marks the Start and End of an algorithm?",["Rectangle","Diamond","Oval (terminal)","Parallelogram"],"C",1,0,"48f2b7f4cb63"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
select public.prepify_load_bank('Computer Science', 3, $j$[["In a professional development team, the person responsible for creating the \"Graphical User Interface (GUI)\" is known as the:",["Front-end Developer.","Back-end Developer.","Database Administrator.","Network Engineer."],"A",3,0,"c8a1e74f71a8"],["What is the functional difference between the starting tag <tag> and the ending tag in HTML?",["The ending tag uses a backslash \\.","The ending tag is recognized with the help of a forward slash /.","The starting tag must be in capital letters.","There is no difference between them."],"B",3,0,"2518f5e96114"],["What is the official file extension required for a browser to recognize a document as an HTML file?",["txt","doc","html","web"],"C",3,0,"149773867ac3"],["Where must all the \"main constituents\" of an HTML document be arranged?",["Inside the <head> tag-pair.","Inside the <body> tag-pair.","Before the <html> tag.","Inside the title section."],"B",3,0,"a715f7ff07af"],["What is the functional difference between <span> and <div> in text arrangement?",["Span provides style to a single line; Div provides it to a set of lines.","Div is for images; Span is for text.","Span is for the header; Div is for the footer.","There is no difference; they are interchangeable."],"A",3,0,"1a62e7848755"],["Which tag-pair should be used if you want to emphasize a word specifically with \"italics\" as a note?",["<b>","<i>","<u>","<sub>"],"B",3,0,"3d3df46bd5bd"],["In the text \"Strong character,\" which tag-pair is officially used for the display of \"bold and strong characters\"?",["<em>","<small>","<strong>","<sup>"],"C",3,0,"1db447853593"],["If a developer wants a heading that is \"largest and most important,\" which level should they choose?",["Level 1 (h1)","Level 6 (h6)","Level 10 (h10)","Main Level (h0)"],"A",3,1,"4ec49e071ef5"],["According to the DOM tree hierarchy, what does the 'html' node contain?",["Only the images of the site.","Two sub-nodes: 'head' and 'body'.","The web browser's search engine index.","The password for the CRM system."],"B",3,0,"16d289cc6003"],["Which IDE environment is mentioned as being used for the \"Visual Studio version 2022\" examples in the text?",["Netbeans","Microsoft Visual Studio","Notepad","Canva"],"B",3,0,"5c8c19ed5168"],["How many languages can the Microsoft Visual Studio IDE support for writing and running code?",["Only 1 (HTML)","Exactly 10","More than 30","Exactly 100"],"C",3,0,"517693460d1d"],["A developer wants to organize data using bullets of type \"circle\" or \"square.\" Which tag-pair must be used as the parent container?",["<ul>","<ol>","<li>","<dl>"],"A",3,0,"055ace91f1d0"],["In a professional HTML table, which tag-pair is specifically designated to allocate and designate data within a \"Header Row\"?",["<td>","<tr>","<th>","<table>"],"C",3,0,"59354b0aaef6"],["Why is JavaScript considered an ideal language for making webpages dynamic at the \"client-end\"?",["It requires a very high amount of memory to run.","It does not consume much memory and works on any operating system.","It can only be used on Windows-based servers.","It replaces the need for using any HTML tags."],"B",3,0,"a8a5328d68b4"],["In programming, what is the official term for a user action that can be \"sensed\" and triggers a specific task to be done?",["Script","event","Variable","Function"],"B",3,1,"ae07983582fb"],["Which JavaScript function is used to display a notification or message box to inform the user about the result of an action?",["alert()","prompt()","document.write()","console.log()"],"A",3,1,"0db63671aa9a"],["Which JavaScript function allows the program to take input from the user via a message window?",["alert()","prompt()","document.write()","var()"],"B",3,1,"ecd7ce965e64"],["Which JavaScript operator is used when you specifically need the \"remainder\" of a division operation?",["/ (Division)","% (Modulus)","* (Multiplication)","+ (Addition)"],"B",3,0,"c8978f8a2222"],["What is the purpose of the comparison operator != in a selection statement?",["To check if two values are equal.","To check if two values are not equal.","To check if the left value is greater.","To check if the right value is smaller."],"B",3,0,"9a9b2a7cd8a1"],["In a selection scenario where there are \"more than two possibilities,\" which structure should be used to extend the logic?",["if statement","if-else statement","if-else if-else statement","For Loop"],"C",3,0,"ef48c42d5189"],["What is the primary advantage of using an \"Iterative Statement\" like a For Loop?",["It makes the code more difficult to read.","The same task is achieved in much lesser lines of code.","It prevents the computer from using any memory.","It only works for mathematical calculations."],"B",3,0,"b575f3fd6a0a"],["In a For Loop, which three components must be set to control the number of iterations?",["Start, Stop, and Pause.","Initialization, terminating condition, and step-size.","HTML, CSS, and JS.","Input, Process, and Output."],"B",3,0,"cf5ec054470a"],["What is the starting \"index number\" for any array declared in JavaScript?",["0","1","-1","10"],"A",3,0,"b5bd5bd70780"],["Which debugging command allows a programmer to trace the code \"line by line\"?",["Start Debugging","Step Into","Toggle Breakpoint","Restart"],"B",3,1,"2b6d89fbb4f9"],["When a programmer wants to add a note in the code that is \"not part of the output\" and is \"ignored by the browser,\" they use:",["Tags","comments","Breakpoints","Alerts"],"B",3,1,"18806fb6eab4"],["According to the DOM tree hierarchy, which node is located at the \"absolute top\" for a whole webpage?",["Document","html","head","body"],"A",3,0,"d37b9db6c850"],["Which of the following is the correct order of priority of CSS styles if all three are used in a webpage?",["External CSS → Embedded CSS → Inline CSS","Embedded CSS → External CSS → Inline CSS","Inline CSS → Embedded CSS → External CSS","Embedded CSS → Inline CSS → External CSS"],"C",3,0,"172405c818b3"],["Which CSS method is recommended for large projects?",["Inline CSS","Embedded CSS","External CSS","Internal CSS"],"C",3,0,"8789e235353c"],["If a user is unable to recall the specific URL of a webpage, which tool creates \"different combinations\" based on keywords to locate it?",["Web Browser","Search Engine","Web Hosting Service","Hyper-Text Markup Language"],"B",3,1,"6af60d958f35"],["What is the first step to establishing a digital presence?",["Website Development","Visual Studio Installation","Writing JavaScript","Buying a Web Server"],"A",3,0,"ca34b3300cd8"],["What is a website called if the information is changed or adjusted in accordance with user input or choice?",["Static Website","Dynamic Website","Single Page Website","Offline Website"],"B",3,0,"fc9aaa3168ff"],["Which of these can be declared as a valid JavaScript variable name without a naming error?",["2myVariable","my-variable","my_variable","my variable"],"C",3,0,"97f76a642af4"],["The value of a variable can change while a program runs, whereas the value of a constant:",["can only be changed by special functions","remains the same throughout the program","changes automatically with the data type","can be changed once per minute"],"B",1,0,"f16e45cb1a99"],["What is the output of document.write(15 % 4) in JavaScript?",["3.75","4","3","1"],"C",5,0,"6e98b004d157"],["Giving a single name to a collection of related elements of the same data type is called:",["An array","A function","A loop","A variable"],"A",1,0,"b92c91174383"],["Which of these JavaScript operators is NOT a logical operator?",["&&","||","!","+"],"D",3,0,"bba836b36c01"],["What happens when the condition of an if statement is valid but evaluates to false?",["The program terminates immediately","Control passes to the statement right after the if block","The condition is evaluated forever","A syntax error stops the program"],"B",5,0,"f0017cf3da89"],["A web developer wants a video to work in as many browsers as possible. Which video format should be preferred?",["AVI","MOV","MP4","WMV"],"C",3,1,"a7cb8a5e003d"],["What is the purpose of the return statement inside a JavaScript function?",["To stop the whole program","To print text on the screen","To send a value back to the caller","To declare a new variable"],"C",3,0,"7723e867ac4b"],["A page contains <p id=\"intro\">Hello</p>. Which JavaScript statement correctly reaches this paragraph through the DOM?",["document.getElement(\"intro\")","document.getElementById(\"intro\")","document.id(\"intro\")","document.findById(\"intro\")"],"B",3,1,"4444655a463a"],["In the HTML page <html><head><title>My Page</title></head><body><h1>Welcome</h1></body></html>, the parent of the <title> element in the DOM tree is:",["<html>","<body>","<head>","<h1>"],"C",5,0,"31265308ffb8"],["Which software development activity focuses on locating and correcting errors after a program has been written?",["Writing the code for the first time","Debugging","Designing the user interface","Translating the program into machine language"],"B",1,0,"bde8534ce3a8"],["A program runs without syntax errors but produces the wrong output. This is most likely a:",["Compilation error","Logical error","Typing error","Installation error"],"B",3,1,"7e69692fa844"],["How many times does the loop for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) run?",["0","2","3","4"],"C",5,0,"fda711a785a2"],["A student writes two sentences on separate lines in the HTML body without any tag between them. How will the page most likely display them?",["On separate lines","As a browser error","On the same line","With the second sentence hidden"],"C",5,1,"64918e1c2acf"],["Which JavaScript data type is designed to hold the result of a logical expression?",["Integer","String","Float","Boolean"],"D",1,0,"bb1624748319"],["Although HTML uses tags and elements, its main purpose is to:",["Perform arithmetic calculations","Define the structure and content of web pages","Store records in a database","Run loops and conditions"],"B",3,0,"ec33165380ad"],["Which CSS property changes the background colour of an element?",["color","bgcolor","background-color","text-color"],"C",1,0,"1bd3221f47af"],["Which JavaScript method writes text directly into the HTML document?",["console.log()","alert()","document.write()","prompt()"],"C",1,0,"333343382470"],["A ticket counter charges 50 if the user's age is 60 or above, and 100 otherwise. Which programming structure suits this logic best?",["A loop","An if-else decision","An array","A sequential structure"],"B",3,1,"cc1d6cdb3ffb"],["A school admits children who are at least 4 years old using the code: var kid_age = 4; if (kid_age > 4) { document.write(\"Admission Granted\"); }. What happens when kid_age is 4?",["\"Admission Granted\" is printed","Nothing is printed","An error occurs because else is missing","\"Admission Granted\" is printed twice"],"B",5,1,"c4af6131f557"],["A program prints \"Excellent\" if score > 80, else \"Good\" if score > 60. A student scores 75. What is printed?",["Excellent","Good","Nothing","Error"],"B",3,1,"7b8c9a57eb2e"],["A shopping list is stored as cart = ['Book', 'Pen', 'Eraser']. How is the second item (\"Pen\") accessed?",["cart[1]","cart[2]","cart(\"Pen\")","cart[0]"],"A",5,1,"cbbd1dc24b4f"],["A student wants to display the numbers 1 to 100 on the screen. Which statement is most efficient for this repetitive task?",["if statement","do...while loop","for loop","switch statement"],"C",3,1,"3c7da4cc84a4"],["In function add(a, b) { return a + b; }, what are a and b called?",["Return values","Parameters","Arrays","Strings"],"B",3,0,"f05c807cb3fe"],["In <p> Hello World </p>, what is the role of p?",["Attribute","Tag","Property","Variable"],"B",1,0,"f469b03ff6d0"],["To make all text inside <div id=\"main\">Text</div> blue, which CSS selector targets this div?",[".main","#main","div.main","*main"],"B",3,1,"21964910cc16"],["A traffic-light program sets light = \"Green\" and then checks if (light == \"Red\") to print \"Stop\". What happens?",["It prints \"Go\"","It prints \"Stop\"","It prints \"Wait\"","It does nothing"],"D",3,1,"36a66e362ef8"],["A program writes average = sum / totalNumbers to find the average of three numbers. This line represents which programming concept?",["Input","Output","Processing","Conditional"],"C",3,1,"83b555d2fe85"],["Your JavaScript runs without any error message but gives a wrong calculation result. What type of error is this?",["Syntax error","Logical error","Reference error","Compilation error"],"B",3,1,"972df260b4a6"],["A page uses <video width=\"500px\" height=\"500px\"><source src=\"video.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video>. The video shows, but the user cannot pause it or change the volume. What is the most likely reason?",["The width and height are too large","The controls attribute is missing from the <video> tag","The source tag should be outside the <video> tag","The file should be .avi"],"B",5,1,"ab6d9e2e29ab"],["How many times does the loop for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) run?",["4","5","6","1"],"B",5,0,"fda711a785a2"],["How many times does the loop for (let i = 0; i < 10; i += 2) run?",["4","5","10","6"],"B",5,0,"fda711a785a2"],["In the JavaScript array let colours = [\"red\", \"green\", \"blue\"];, the value of colours[1] is:",["\"red\"","\"green\"","\"blue\"","undefined"],"B",5,0,"b5bd5bd70780"],["A shop uses the code: var amount = 500; if (amount >= 500) { document.write(\"Discount!\"); }. What happens?",["\"Discount!\" is printed","Nothing is printed","An error occurs","\"500\" is printed"],"A",5,1,"c4af6131f557"],["What is the value of 17 % 5 in JavaScript?",["3","2","3.4","12"],"B",5,0,"c8978f8a2222"],["Which JavaScript function shows a dialog box with a text field so that the user can type a value?",["alert()","confirm()","prompt()","document.write()"],"C",3,0,"ecd7ce965e64"],["To show a message inside the web page itself rather than in a pop-up, a beginner can use:",["alert()","document.write()","prompt()","confirm()"],"B",3,0,"333343382470"],["Which HTML heading tag displays the smallest head